// How the Solar System formed, drawn (solarFormation.js gives the dates):
// - the collapsing cloud core: a dark dust globule, opaque enough to blot out the Milky Way behind it;
// - the protoplanetary disk around the young Sun, ~100 au across: dust lit by the star (bright and warm near it,
//   dimmer and redder outward), gaps opening where the giant planets grow (as ALMA images show in young disks such as
//   HL Tau), a speckle of planetesimals; then, once the gas has gone, a faint debris disk;
// - the Earth through its history: molten while it grows and after the Moon-forming impact, a dark crust before the
//   oceans, an orange methane haze at times before oxygen, the ice of Snowball Earth; the continents are drawn as
//   they are today (plate tectonics has rearranged them many times: not modelled);
// - the ring of hot debris around the Earth after the impact, from which the Moon gathers.
